  "provider_query": "Python standard library documentation for the venv module",
  "answer": "Official and closely related pages for Python’s standard-library `venv` module:\n\n1. **[venv — Creation of virtual environments](https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html)** — Current stable library reference (CLI, options, `EnvBuilder` API). Source: docs.python.org.\n\n2. **[venv — Python 3.14.1 library docs](https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/venv.html)** — Versioned library page (added in 3.3; creation command, flags, API). Source: docs.python.org.\n\n3. **[12. Virtual Environments and Packages](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/venv.html)** — Tutorial: create, activate, and use a venv (`.venv`, `python -m venv`). Source: docs.python.org.\n\n4. **[venv library docs (3.10.2 snapshot)](https://docs.python.org/3/library/venv.html)** — Same module docs with activation table (bash, fish, csh, cmd, PowerShell) and PEP 405 note. Source: docs.python.org.\n\n5. **[Tutorial source (venv.rst)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/HEAD/Doc/tutorial/venv.rst)** — CPython repo source for the tutorial chapter. Source: python/cpython on GitHub.\n\n6. **[venv: Python Built-in Virtual Environment Module](https://pydevtools.com/handbook/reference/venv/)** — Short handbook summary vs virtualenv/uv and common flags. Source: pydevtools.\n\n7. **[Python venv: How To Create, Activate, Deactivate, And Delete](https://python.land/virtual-environments/virtualenv)** — Practical walkthrough that links to the official docs. Source: Python Land.\n\n8. **[Python venv — virtual environments using venv](https://zetcode.com/python/venv/)** — Short tutorial on create/activate and directory layout (`pyvenv.cfg`, site-packages). Source: ZetCode.",
